<title>KAZAKHSTAN: Kazakh 3-mth T-bill avg yield falls to 13.10 pct.</title>
<headline>Kazakh 3-mth T-bill avg yield falls to 13.10 pct.</headline>
<dateline>ALMATY 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield on an issue of three-month MKM discount Treasury bills fell to 13.10 percent at an auction on July 1 from 13.18 percent at the previous auction on June 24, the National Bank said.</p>
<p>Details of the auction:</p>
<p>					   July 1	     June 24</p>
<p> Series number			 KZ43K0210973     KZ43K2509976</p>
<p> Issue volume (mln tenge)	  500		  500</p>
<p> Bids (nominal, mln tenge)	 2,057		991</p>
<p> Sold (nominal)			507		  500</p>
<p> Average price			 96.83 pct	  96.81 pct</p>
<p> Average yield			 13.10		13.18</p>
<p> Tenor				   91 days	    91 days</p>
<p> Maturity				Oct 2, 1997	Sep 25, 1997</p>
<p>--Almaty Newsroom, +7 3272 509410</p>
